    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Regarding that \"weaving conflict\" and driver behavior you mentioned—how do we quantify those unpredictable human elements in the model? I'm trying to understand why certain junctions experience sudden, erratic drops in throughput that don't seem to follow the expected queuing models. Is there a way to model that kind of \"random\" friction mathematically?",
