      "content": "Quantifying unpredictable human elements is a challenge, as it's inherently less deterministic than traffic flow itself. You can model this \"random friction\" by incorporating stochastic elements into your simulation, perhaps using probabilistic distributions for gap acceptance times or driver aggressiveness. Instead of assuming perfect adherence to rules, you introduce variance—like a random variable representing the likelihood of a driver hesitating or making an overly assertive maneuver. This allows the model to capture the sudden, erratic drops in throughput you are observing.",
